{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The issue was in `percentile` in `repo/stats.py`. It used `int(p / 100 * n)` as a 0-based index, which is one rank too high for nearest-rank percentiles. For 1..10 at p50 that gave index 5 → **6** instead of **5**.\n\n**Fix:** Use the standard nearest-rank rule: sort the values, compute 1-based rank `ceil(p / 100 * n)`, and take `ordered[rank - 1]`. Handle `p <= 0` and `p >= 100` as min and max.\n\n**Cleanup:** Removed the incorrect inline comment, dropped unused `old_percentile`, and added a small `math.ceil` import.\n\n`repo/aggregate.py` already calls `percentile` for p50/p90/p99 in `summarize()`, so those summaries pick up the fix automatically. All visible tests pass (`python -m pytest tests/visible -q`)."}]},"session_id":"a02df3db-e8d8-453f-9d69-48a53416e292"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":40740,"duration_api_ms":40740,"is_error":false,"result":"Exploring the stats module and related code to fix percentile calculations and clean up the reporting CLI stats.\n\n\nFixing nearest-rank percentile: use `ceil(p/100 * n) - 1` instead of `int(p/100 * n)`, which overshoots for p=50 on n=10.\n\n\nThe issue was in `percentile` in `repo/stats.py`. It used `int(p / 100 * n)` as a 0-based index, which is one rank too high for nearest-rank percentiles. For 1..10 at p50 that gave index 5 → **6** instead of **5**.\n\n**Fix:** Use the standard nearest-rank rule: sort the values, compute 1-based rank `ceil(p / 100 * n)`, and take `ordered[rank - 1]`. Handle `p <= 0` and `p >= 100` as min and max.\n\n**Cleanup:** Removed the incorrect inline comment, dropped unused `old_percentile`, and added a small `math.ceil` import.\n\n`repo/aggregate.py` already calls `percentile` for p50/p90/p99 in `summarize()`, so those summaries pick up the fix automatically. All visible tests pass (`python -m pytest tests/visible -q`).","session_id":"a02df3db-e8d8-453f-9d69-48a53416e292","request_id":"43dac162-eab1-4688-86f9-e319e06f21da","usage":{"inputTokens":13442,"outputTokens":2282,"cacheReadTokens":79491,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
